menu "SensorStation3"

    config SS3_USE_BSEC
        bool "Enable BSEC air-quality processing for BME680"
        default n
        help
            Links the precompiled Bosch BSEC library and enables IAQ/CO2eq/VOC
            processing when a BME680 sensor is detected. Requires the
            precompiled libalgobsec.a for the ESP32 Xtensa LX6 target.

            When disabled, the bsec component is excluded from the build
            entirely (not compiled, not linked). BME680 sensors still report
            temperature/humidity/pressure/gas resistance and an approximate
            CO2eq (via bmx280's built-in gas-resistance estimate), but without
            BSEC's IAQ/static_iaq/accuracy outputs.

    choice SS3_LCD_PANEL
        prompt "LCD panel driver"
        default SS3_LCD_PANEL_AUTO
        help
            SensorStation3 supports both ILI9341 and ST7789 SPI panels, which
            share identical wiring on the CYD board. By default the panel
            controller is auto-detected at boot by reading the display's ID
            register (RDDID). Force a specific driver here if auto-detection
            picks the wrong one for your module.

        config SS3_LCD_PANEL_AUTO
            bool "Auto-detect (read panel ID at boot)"

        config SS3_LCD_PANEL_ILI9341
            bool "Force ILI9341"

        config SS3_LCD_PANEL_ST7789
            bool "Force ST7789"

    endchoice

endmenu